<title>FRANCE: Alcatel board nominates directors.</title>
<headline>Alcatel board nominates directors.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>French telecommunications and engineering group Alcatel Alsthom said on Monday that its board would propose eight directors at the annual shareholders meeting on June 19.</p>
<p>It said in a statement the board would propose the renewal of four board members, chairman Serge Tchuruk, Ambroise Roux, Societe Generale chairman Marc Vienot and Rand Araskog of ITT.</p>
<p>It proposed four new directors, Carrefour chairman Daniel Bernard, former Mercedez Benz chief executive Helmut Werner, Valeo chairman Noel Goutard and Philippe Bissara, who is about to leave his job as the group's general secretary.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
